/**
 * @component banner
 * @summary A dismissible, iconed message surface for page-level or in-context announcements.
 * @remarks
 *   **Size** controls padding and gap: `relaxed` (default) is roomier; `compact` tightens both.
 *   **Color** sets the fill: bare (no modifier) is unfilled — border and icon only; `-color-violet`
 *   and `-color-sea` add a tinted background plus a matching icon swatch.
 * @selector .pfx-banner
 * @annotations
 * 1. Banner renders an `info` glyph by default. Add `-icon-<name>` to swap it for any glyph from the shared icon set.
 * 2. The close button follows `alert`'s top-end positioning. It defaults to small; add a size modifier to override it.
 * 3. A heading (`h1`–`h6`, or a bare `.pfx-heading` with no `-level-*` modifier) styles as the
 *    banner's title, using title-card typography appropriate to the active size. Give an
 *    `.pfx-heading` a `-level-*` class to opt it out of this treatment.
 * 4. Wrap banner actions in `.button-group`: buttons before the last default to the inline secondary
 *    treatment, and the last button defaults to the inline primary treatment. Add a `-color-*`
 *    modifier to any button to use its own colour.
 * 5. Buttons default to `-size-sm` regardless of the banner's own size; add a `-size-*` modifier to
 *    opt out.
 * @modifier -size-relaxed — Roomier padding and gap (default).
 * @modifier -size-compact — Tighter padding and gap.
 * @modifier -size-sm - @alias {@link -size-compact}
 * @modifier -size-md - @alias {@link -size-relaxed}
 * @modifier -color-violet — Violet-tinted background and icon swatch.
 * @modifier -color-sea — Sea-tinted background and icon swatch.
 * @modifier -icon-* — Swap the default `info` glyph for an icon from the shared icon set (for example, `-icon-megaphone`).
 * @part button-group — The row container for banner action buttons.
 * @structure
 * .pfx-banner {
 *   @component heading:optional {}
 *   slot {}
 *   @variant bare-button {
 *     @component button:max-1 {}
 *   }
 *   @variant button-group {
 *     .button-group {
 *       @component button:one-or-more:max-2 {}
 *     }
 *   }
 *   @component close-button:optional {}
 * }
 * @a11y Add `role="status"` (or `role="alert"` for urgent messages) so assistive tech announces the
 *   banner; mark a decorative icon `aria-hidden="true"` and give the close button an `aria-label`.
 * @usage @import "@pantoken/plugin-custom-components/custom-components.css";
